  "summary": "Dieter Rams's Braun design system: neutral surfaces, few controls, ordered grids and the doctrine \"Weniger, aber besser.\"",
  "description": "As Braun's design chief from 1955, Dieter Rams (with Gugelot and the Ulm school lineage) created radios, record players and calculators of almost-invisible clarity: white or black boxes, one accent color, gridded controls, honest materials. His ten principles of good design and \"less, but better\" became modernism's late canon — famously echoed in Jony Ive's Apple. It remains the benchmark of restraint in industrial design.",
